From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:04:14 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 09/48] net: xpon: omci: stay on the baseline message set

The agent decodes extended OMCI messages (device identifier 0x0b), but
the Get response of every managed entity except ME 341 and the MIB
upload next response are only built in the baseline layout: an extended
Get answer put the attribute values where G.988 expects the two failure
masks, and an extended MIB upload next answer was a baseline record.

ONU2-G advertises 0xa0 by default (G.988 2010, baseline only), so an OLT
should not send extended messages, but the OMCC version could be set to
any non-zero value through sysfs or the netlink configuration, including
the code points that announce the extended set.

Refuse those code points (0x96 and 0xb0-0xbf) as OMCC version and ignore
extended requests, counting them as unsupported, instead of answering
them with malformed contents.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 net/xpon/omci/agent.c | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/xpon/omci/agent.c b/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
index 025dc95..45f1066 100644
--- a/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
+++ b/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
@@ -200,6 +200,15 @@ static bool omci_agent_result_can_be_faked(u8 result)
 #define OMCI_OLT_G_EQUIPMENT_ID_MASK	0x4000
 #define OMCI_OLT_G_VERSION_MASK	0x2000
 #define OMCI_OMCC_VERSION_G988_2010_BASELINE	0xa0
+
+/*
+ * G.988 ONU2-G OMCC version code points: 0x96 and 0xb0-0xbf announce the
+ * extended message set as well as the baseline one.
+ */
+static bool omci_omcc_version_extended(u8 version)
+{
+	return version == 0x96 || (version & 0xf0) == 0xb0;
+}
 #define OMCI_OLT_G_TIME_OF_DAY_MASK	0x1000
 #define OMCI_OLT_G_TIME_OF_DAY_LEN	14
 
@@ -4897,6 +4906,19 @@ void omci_agent_receive(struct omci_device *odev, const struct sk_buff *skb)
 	if (ret)
 		return;
 	omci_agent_log_wire(odev, "RX", skb->data, skb->len);
+	/*
+	 * ONU2-G advertises a baseline-only OMCC version, and several
+	 * responses (Get, MIB upload next) are only built in the baseline
+	 * layout: an extended message would get a malformed answer.
+	 */
+	if (request.device_id == OMCI_EXTENDED_DEV_ID) {
+		dev_dbg(odev->parent,
+			"OMCI extended message ignored: tci=%#06x type=%#04x class=%u\n",
+			request.transaction_id, request.message_type,
+			request.class_id);
+		atomic64_inc(&agent->unsupported);
+		return;
+	}
 	ani_g_test = omci_agent_is_ani_g_test(&request);
 	request_hash = jhash(skb->data, skb->len, 0);
 
@@ -5397,7 +5419,7 @@ __omci_agent_config_set_source(struct omci_device *odev, u16 key,
 			break;
 		}
 		scalar = *(const u8 *)value;
-		if (!scalar) {
+		if (!scalar || omci_omcc_version_extended(scalar)) {
 			ret = -EINVAL;
 			break;
 		}
